### escaped field reference passed to awk
alias fields='awk "{print \$1}"'
>>- SC2142 1:7 -- the alias body escapes the dollar, so awk receives $1 and the shell never reads a positional parameter

### escaped dollar in the alias body
alias price='echo \$1'
>>- SC2142 1:7 -- the alias body escapes the dollar, so echo prints $1 literally

### awk program single-quoted inside the alias body
alias names='ls -l | awk '"'"'{print $9}'"'"
>>- SC2142 1:7 -- the $9 sits in single quotes inside the alias body, so awk reads it and the shell never does

### positional parameter of a function the alias defines
alias greet='hello() { echo "hi $1"; }; hello'
>>- SC2142 1:7 -- $1 belongs to the function the alias defines and calls, which receives the alias arguments

### shell name in an alias
alias me='echo $0'
>>- SC2142 1:7 -- $0 names the shell rather than a positional parameter

### length of a positional parameter in an alias
alias len='echo ${#1}'
>>+ SC2142 1:7 -- ${#1} reads the first positional parameter too; shellcheck only matches $1 and ${1
